                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                        "entry_id": "f4140b0d-c01a-3b41-a7b4-f82d14eb74da",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not random; caused or manipulated; arranged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6841c9c1-5408-4ba2-96d3-faf84416eb5b",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "The apparent accident was a nonrandom event: someone carefully arranged it to happen when and where it did."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9500b505-4c77-46b0-99a9-75be4102adcf",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "The evidence presented indicates that the regional variations in uranium content in rhyolitic and dacitic rocks are nonrandom in nature."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc2da7c7-e93f-4f81-bf4c-c6559ca6e52b",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "As an example of the method, table 1 summarizes the computations used in estimating the variance of the random component of early fall lettuce yields in California for the years 1918–57. The question is: Beginning with which difference is it reasonably certain that the nonrandom element has been eliminated, leaving an estimate of the random variance?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13fc53d7-d99a-49b3-ac8e-67540344d6e1",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "Confidence intervals can be used to isolate areas of discrepancies if bias exist as being a result of either a 'nonrandom selection technique or a non-representative selection list."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fe7c09f-5328-4855-8db6-c0f007986e1e",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "There is no need to consider those individuals who survive the process of nonrandom elimination to be the products fo a goal-directed process."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac2bb7a6-7eb0-4339-bb73-a5715e0afbdd",
                                "sense_id": "b8a18a82-bcaa-3b2d-b852-f0f2da48b8ef",
                                "text": "However, it should be noted that theoretically, the apparent nonrandom distance of the dispersal has evolved because of its advantage to the species."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
